The project owner's first human playtest of the windowed client (post-M10.1)
produced four findings in priority order: controls, visual legibility, menus
and settings, audio. A14 (the Alpha declaration) is blocked until they are
fixed and re-tested.

This file records the milestone specification verbatim: the global rules
(presentation/input only above the sim boundary, zero golden hash movement,
commit-after-every-small-change, gates per commit, direction-pinning tests
for every input change, ADR + allow-list for new crates, register updates),
the four phases with their exits, and the delivery protocol (local branch
m10.2 from master, never squashed, one format-patch file verified by
git am on a fresh clone of the base commit, then uploaded to the owner's
delivery repository — the token stays out-of-band and out of every file,
commit message, and log).
