The Generals ZH selection half. click_select/box_select split into pure
picks (pick_own_entity, box_pick) plus the release handler's decision:

- Shift+click TOGGLES: an unselected pick joins, a selected pick leaves
  (input::shift_click_selection, order preserved).
- Shift+box ADDS: the box's picks union into the current selection
  instead of replacing it (input::union_selection, no duplicates).
- Double-click on a unit selects all VISIBLE units of the same kind —
  same owner, same kind, fog-filtered view snapshot (input::
  same_kind_selection); a 350 ms window (DOUBLE_CLICK_MS) gates it, and
  shift+double-click unions rather than replaces.
- A single click on EMPTY GROUND does nothing at all now: never an order
  (left never orders — that was already true), and no silent deselect
  either (PLAN §1.1's 'click on empty ground with a selection and
  nothing else = nothing happens'); Escape is the deselect key.

Four unit tests pin the pure functions. Zero golden movement:
presentation/input only.
