Ctrl+digit assigns, digit recalls — and now a double tap of the same
digit inside DOUBLE_TAP_MS (350 ms) recalls AND jumps the camera to the
group's live members' center of mass (input::group_center: dead ids
weigh nothing, a stale group reference is harmless), keeping the current
zoom distance. An assign (Ctrl+digit) breaks the double-tap chain — the
next double tap must be two recalls.

Two unit tests pin the window and the centroid. Zero golden movement:
presentation/input only.
