MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Escape now climbs one rung per press instead of jumping to quit: armed
command, then placement, then the selection, and only with nothing armed,
placed, or selected does it close the window (the old code quit on the
first press whenever nothing was armed — an accidental Esc with units
selected cost the player their window, not just their selection; and
with empty-ground clicks no longer deselecting, Escape is the deselect
key, per the plan's 'Escape cancels an armed command or clears the
selection').

Space (the plan's optional 'jump to the last event or base' — cheap, so
it exists) centers the camera on the most recent DEATH's position, else
the player's start anchor, keeping the zoom distance. Deaths are the
event class a player most wants to look at; attack hits would thrash
the target every combat tick.

Two unit tests pin the ladder order and the fallback. Zero golden
movement: presentation/input only.
---
