Subject: [PATCH 07/13] =?UTF-8?q?feat(client):=20cursor=20order=20feedback?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20=E2=80=94=20the=20ground=20marker=20and=20the=20armed=20cros?=
 =?UTF-8?q?shair=20(PLAN=20=C2=A71.3)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Before pressing, the player now SEES what the next click would do:

- A small marker (filled square in a hollow outline, feedback.rs) at the
  GROUND point under the cursor — it sticks to the world, not the pixel
  — colored by the would-be order: green Move, red Attack, amber
  Gather, blue rally, orange armed attack-move. It resolves through the
  same context-order machinery that issues the order (the single
  selected-producer rally case extracted into
  selection_is_single_producer so both paths agree), so the preview
  cannot lie. Placement mode suppresses it (the ghost is that mode's
  marker) and an empty selection draws nothing — the plan's 'invalid'
  reads cleanest as silence.
- The window cursor becomes a crosshair while attack-move is armed
  (set on change, not per frame).
- The command ping stays: the marker previews, the ping confirms.

The marker's colors avoid the red/green confusion pair by value as
well as hue (the plan's §2.2 color-blind note, applied early because
it is free here). Four unit tests pin the colors, the quad geometry,
and the silences. Zero golden movement: presentation/input only.
